WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.143 --> 00:00:01.300
(pleasant music)

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:05.980
- For 31 years I have been
acting in major motion pictures

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:10.980
and TV series, but you
may not recognize my face.

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:13.570
I'm Doug Jones.

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:14.887
I am an actor.

00:00:14.887 --> 00:00:17.637
(pleasant music)

00:00:20.113 --> 00:00:22.500
(pleasant music)

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:27.500
I got into acting out of a
need, almost, to be validated.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:30.600
And it was at Ball State University that I

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:32.470
discovered the art of mime.

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:33.960
It was a very visual form of

00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:36.020
communication and entertainment.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:38.100
Little did I know that this would be early

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.590
training grounds for the career that I was

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:40.940
going to have in later years.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:41.900
I had no idea.

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:46.760
After moving out to
Hollywood-land in March of 1985,

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:49.210
I'm thinking, “Okay,
now's the time to pursue

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:50.120
“this acting thing.”

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:54.160
My fourth booking was for
a McDonald's campaign.

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:57.090
That got my kinda hooked
into, oh, he's that tall,

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:01.440
skinny guy who wears stuff
and moves well in it,

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.390
and doesn't complain while doing so.

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:07.250
My first feature film was Batman Returns.

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:10.470
I got that audition because
of my contortive legs.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.420
In the credits it says,
Thin Clown, which kind of,

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:15.310
it's kind of self descriptive, isn't it?

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:17.930
I have been in over 150 productions.

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:20.210
That would include everything
from feature films like

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:23.970
“Hocus Pocus,” “Hellboy” One,
“Hellboy II: The Golden Army.”

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:26.310
The faun in “Pan's Labyrinth”
was a page turning

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:27.920
career moment for me.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.330
“Fantastic Four: Rise of
the Silver Surfer”; I played

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:31.163
the Silver Surfer.

00:01:31.163 --> 00:01:33.700
“Star Trek: Discovery as Commander Saru.”

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:35.840
And most recently, “The Shape of Water.”

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:39.520
So when asked about how
long does the makeup take,

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:41.250
it, depending on the creature,
it can be anything

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:44.590
from a suit going on
and zipping up the back

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:47.050
or a makeup that is applied
to you from head to toe.

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:49.860
For instance, as Commander
Saru on “Star Trek: Discovery,”

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:54.210
it's around two hours a day,
which is mercifully short.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:57.180
Flip side would be an Abe
Sapien from the “Hellboy” movies.

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:58.670
So that's one of the longer ones.

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:00.160
That took seven hours a day.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:03.690
Wearing rubber bits that gets everything

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:04.750
that you think it would be.

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:07.260
It is hotter than you
want to be, it is heavier

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.430
than you want it to be,
it is more isolating

00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:12.010
than you want it to be,
you can't always get access

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:14.400
to your naughty bits
to go pee if you want.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.160
Why go through all of
this makeup application,

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.330
the time that it takes?

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:21.210
You can create monsters with VFX now.

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:23.180
I think people like to watch other people,

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:25.860
so even if that person
is playing a monster,

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:28.500
they wanna connect with
a human's interpretation

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:29.990
and performance of that monster.

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:32.590
It's old school cinema magic.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:36.140
I kind of get the best of
both worlds when it comes to

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:38.200
being a public celebrity.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.680
The bigger movies I've been
in, and the bigger things

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:42.500
that I'm known for, I look like this,

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:46.480
and then on the street, I'm
just a tall, skinny guy.

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:47.710
That's a gift.

00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:49.670
Now that I'm in a movie
like “The Shape of Water”

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:52.270
with 13 Oscar nominations, I'm
getting recognized in public

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:53.170
a little bit more.

00:02:54.850 --> 00:02:56.480
But it's still not to the point where I,

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.380
where I have people hiding
in my bushes, hoping

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:00.050
to get a snapshot of me topless.

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:01.244
That's not happening yet.

00:03:01.244 --> 00:03:03.994
(pleasant music)

